Subject: [M152] [compiler] Don't assume a memory fence for generated-code
 feedback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Original change's description:
> [compiler] Don't assume a memory fence for generated-code feedback
>
> Feedback slots written by generated code are published with a plain
> store, so background reads of such values have to keep the
> IsPendingAllocation check.
>
> These incorrectly used MakeRefAssumeMemoryFence:
>
> ReadFeedbackForInstanceOf ic-callable.tq
> ReadFeedbackForArrayOrObjectLiteral CreateEmptyArrayLiteral, in CSA
> ReadFeedbackForTemplateObject internal.tq GetTemplateObject
>
> Use plain TryMakeRef instead.
>
> Fixed: 559780376
> Change-Id: I727e94cda8f858cc84a33309bab6962b9572a8c6
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8425682
> Commit-Queue: Marja Hölttä <marja@chromium.org>
> Reviewed-by: Marja Hölttä <marja@chromium.org>
> Auto-Submit: Jakob Linke <jgruber@chromium.org>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#109982}

(cherry picked from commit ec136c5038d337396e362db4c9a4198ffda0d1ed)

